  "hints": [
    {
      "tr": "Dersteki `psi` fonksiyonunu satırlardan değer çekecek biçimde uyarla: `sorted(r[name] for r in reference)`.",
      "en": "Adapt the lesson's `psi` function to pull values from rows: `sorted(r[name] for r in reference)`."
    },
    {
      "tr": "İç fonksiyon `shares(rows)` sütun adını dışarıdaki `name`'den görür; her sütunda yeniden tanımlanır.",
      "en": "The inner function `shares(rows)` sees the column name from the outer `name`; it is redefined for every column."
    },
    {
      "tr": "Çözümün tamamı:\n\n```python\nimport bisect\nimport math\n\n\ndef drift_report(reference, current, columns, bins):\n    report = []\n    for name in columns:\n        ordered = sorted(r[name] for r in reference)\n        edges = [ordered[len(ordered) * i // bins] for i in range(1, bins)]\n\n        def shares(rows):\n            counts = [0] * bins\n            for r in rows:\n                counts[bisect.bisect_left(edges, r[name])] += 1\n            return [max(c / len(rows), 0.0001) for c in counts]\n\n        ref, cur = shares(reference), shares(current)\n        value = sum((c - r) * math.log(c / r) for r, c in zip(ref, cur))\n        if value < 0.1:\n            label = \"stable\"\n        elif value <= 0.25:\n            label = \"moderate\"\n        else:\n            label = \"large\"\n        report.append([name, round(value, 3), label])\n    return report\n\n\nreference = [{\"fee\": f, \"calls\": c} for f, c in zip(range(20, 40), [0, 1] * 10)]\ncurrent = [{\"fee\": f + 8, \"calls\": c} for f, c in zip(range(20, 40), [0, 1] * 10)]\nfor row in drift_report(reference, current, [\"fee\", \"calls\"], 4):\n    print(row)\n```",
      "en": "The full solution:\n\n```python\nimport bisect\nimport math\n\n\ndef drift_report(reference, current, columns, bins):\n    report = []\n    for name in columns:\n        ordered = sorted(r[name] for r in reference)\n        edges = [ordered[len(ordered) * i // bins] for i in range(1, bins)]\n\n        def shares(rows):\n            counts = [0] * bins\n            for r in rows:\n                counts[bisect.bisect_left(edges, r[name])] += 1\n            return [max(c / len(rows), 0.0001) for c in counts]\n\n        ref, cur = shares(reference), shares(current)\n        value = sum((c - r) * math.log(c / r) for r, c in zip(ref, cur))\n        if value < 0.1:\n            label = \"stable\"\n        elif value <= 0.25:\n            label = \"moderate\"\n        else:\n            label = \"large\"\n        report.append([name, round(value, 3), label])\n    return report\n\n\nreference = [{\"fee\": f, \"calls\": c} for f, c in zip(range(20, 40), [0, 1] * 10)]\ncurrent = [{\"fee\": f + 8, \"calls\": c} for f, c in zip(range(20, 40), [0, 1] * 10)]\nfor row in drift_report(reference, current, [\"fee\", \"calls\"], 4):\n    print(row)\n```"
    }
